# LIQUID-11 — Prefer Liquid array filters over manual loops

## Rationale

Shopify Liquid provides array filters (`find`, `where`, `map`, `first`, etc.)
that are clearer and often more efficient than hand-written search loops.

## How to check

Look for `{% for %}` blocks that iterate an array only to find one item by a
property, test membership, or extract values.

## How to fix

Replace the loop with the appropriate array filter.

## Examples

### Bad

```liquid
{% assign current_color_value = '' %}
{% assign color_option_values = product.options_with_values[color_index].values %}
{% for value in color_option_values %}
  {% if value.name == current_color %}
    {% assign current_color_value = value.swatch.color %}
    {% break %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
```

### Good

```liquid
{% assign current_color_option = product.options_with_values[color_index].values | find: 'name', current_color %}
{% assign current_color_value = current_color_option.swatch.color.rgb %}
```

### Common filters

| Goal | Filter |
|------|--------|
| Find one item by property | `\| find: 'property', value` |
| Filter array | `\| where: 'property', value` |
| Extract property list | `\| map: 'property'` |
| Test membership | `\| has: 'property', value` |
| Remove nils | `\| compact` |
